{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtWkmfxfJGSdrGApQKRL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A memory write no longer evicts the static instructions. The fix is in `bot.py`, and I wrote the details to `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `build_system()` put the coaching instructions and the athlete's facts list in one block marked `cache_control`. Caching matches the prompt prefix byte for byte, so each `save_fact` changed the prefix and the next request paid full price to rewrite it. The usage log shows exactly that pattern.\n\n**Change:** `build_system()` now returns two blocks:\n- **Cached:** instructions plus the stable athlete profile (name, sport, zones, goal, language). The `cache_control` marker is here.\n- **Uncached:** today's date and the facts list, placed after the cache breakpoint.\n\nA memory write or a new day now changes only the uncached block. The old `athlete_context()` helper is replaced by `athlete_profile()` and `athlete_memory()`. Nothing else in the repo calls it.\n\n**Verification:**\n- New `test_prompt_cache.py` has 5 tests, all passing. On the original code 4 of them fail.\n- An end-to-end run through `reply()` with a fake LLM confirmed the cached block is identical before and after a `save_fact`.\n- I have not checked this against the live API, since there is no key here. After deploy, check the next `logs/usage.jsonl` entries after a save: `cache_read_input_tokens` should hold steady and there should be no new cache creation.\n\n**Caveats (details in ANSWER.md):**\n- **Minimum cacheable size:** the cached prefix may now sit near the API's 1024-token minimum. If it falls below, caching silently stops. Check `cache_creation_input_tokens` on the first call for each athlete. I did not pad the prompt.\n- **Tool selection also breaks the cache:** tool definitions come before the system prompt in the prefix, and `select_tools()` changes the tool list by keyword. Messages containing \"plan\" or \"race\" miss the cache even without a memory write, as the `plan_week` row in the log shows. I left this alone because it trades against the March filtering win in `NOTES.md`. The options are to always send the full tool list, or to accept misses on keyword messages.\n\nI did not commit anything. Changes are in `bot.py`, `test_prompt_cache.py` (new), and `ANSWER.md` (new)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1632,"cache_read_input_tokens":38967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1632},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c844f66b-7d49-4f5c-9839-d41f54baf4e9","uuid":"3b8c4592-2b72-43e8-b563-f5690856c4d9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:10:27.518Z","request_id":"req_011CgtWkmW344miuS8LnQN5k"}
